<LegalLayout title="Terms of Service" heading="Terms of Service" description="Terms of Service for Public IPTV trials and subscriptions: lawful use, accounts, billing, availability, termination and liability.">
  <p>
    These terms govern free trials and paid subscriptions from Public IPTV
    (“we”, “our”). By requesting a trial or using a subscription, you agree to
    them. Questions: contact@public-iptv.online.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    We provide television over internet protocol: live channel categories
    (sports, movies, news, kids, international), video on demand where offered,
    and a program guide, playable in any compatible M3U playlist player. Every
    plan starts with a free trial so you can verify the lineup on your own
    devices before paying.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">2. Lawful use and eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    You must be old enough to enter contracts in your country, use the service
    for personal, non-commercial viewing, and comply with local law. You may not
    resell, restream, publish or redistribute our streams or credentials, probe
    our infrastructure, or use the service to infringe anyone's rights. We may
    suspend accounts that breach this section.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">3. Accounts and connections</h2>
  <p>
    Your login is personal: keep it confidential and notify us of suspected
    misuse. Each plan allows an agreed number of simultaneous screens, confirmed
    in writing when your login is created. Sharing logins beyond that limit may
    lead to temporary restriction and, if repeated, termination without refund.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">4. Billing</h2>
  <p>
    Plan lengths, prices and renewal dates are confirmed in writing before
    anything is charged — nothing is ever billed silently. Monthly plans renew
    until cancelled; longer plans do not auto-convert to a different length.
    You can cancel future renewals at any time by email; cancellation stops the
    next charge but does not retrospectively refund time already used, except as
    the refund policy provides.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">5. Quality and availability</h2>
  <p>
    Streams are delivered best-effort over the public internet. We work to keep
    feeds stable, including 4K where your connection supports it (about 25 Mbps
    per 4K screen, 10 Mbps per HD screen), but we do not promise uninterrupted,
    error-free viewing: maintenance, upstream outages and local network problems
    can interrupt service. If a paid plan persistently fails and support cannot
    fix it, the refund policy applies.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">6. Suspension and termination</h2>
  <p>
    We may suspend or terminate service for breach of these terms, payment
    failure or fraud, after where reasonable contacting you first. You may
    terminate at any time by cancelling renewal and letting the paid period
    expire.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">7. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, our liability for any claim arising
    from the service is limited to the amount you paid for the current billing
    period. Nothing here limits rights you hold under consumer law, which always
    prevail over these terms where they conflict.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Material changes are published on this page with a new date and, for
    account-holding customers, announced by email before taking effect.
  </p>
  <p>Last updated: 2026-10-04.</p>
</LegalLayout>
